The Titans (led by Kronos) were defeated by the Olympians (led by Zeus,
son of Kronos).  Some of the Titans were allowed to "become" Olympians
with certain conditions to  their surrender.
Basically they were not allowed as much say in what the other gods
did, but were none the less immortal.  I believe Neptune and his daughter
were Titans, however, they helped Zeus defeat his father.
Kronos, the Titan leader, was castrated and cast off Mount Olympos by Zeus.

